<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via two-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via two-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves to the banking system on Tuesday via a round of two-day fixed system repurchase agreements, said a spokeswoman at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York.</p>
<p>At 1030/1430 GMT, the time the Fed usually intervenes in the market, federal funds were trading at 5-5/16 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>-- (( N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660 ))</p>
</text>
